that only very experienced GMs can compensate for.<br /> <br /> A massive rewrite by someone with a gift for simple flexible mechanics and evocative settings would be a wonderful thing.<br /> <br /> C:tD, C:tL, and DA:F all do highly distinctive and interesting takes on the Faeries. But DA:Fae is totally limited by its rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T20:04:42-07:00","id":1519555,"title":"","content":"I love DA: Fae. I love the ideas on display. The powers are this cool intersection of Gift-like specificity, Discipline-like progression, and Sphere- (really Pillar-)like flexibility. Fae society is rich and supernatural, but in a way that feels organically compatible with other WoD stories.<br /> <br /> But... yeah, when you start looking too close, there's a lot there that doesn't quite *work*. But I really want it to work! So I make allowances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}